# @motion-canvas/vite-plugin@3.17.2 declares `peerDependencies: {vite: "4.x || 5.x"}`
# and has not published a release that widens it (3.18.0-alpha.0 still says the same).
# This project runs vite 6 anyway, deliberately: vite 5 resolves esbuild 0.21, which is
# inside the GHSA-67mh-4wv8-2f99 range (<=0.24.2, any website can issue requests to the
# dev server and read the response) and has no fix on the 5.x line. vite 6 requires
# esbuild ^0.25.0, which clears it.
#
# Without this flag npm refuses the tree with ERESOLVE. Verified under vite 6.4.3:
# `vite build` produces the same three chunks at the same sizes as under vite 5, and the
# dev server starts with BOTH plugins initialized — the ffmpeg exporter binds `server.ws`
# in `configureServer`, which vite 6 still provides.
#
# NOT verified: a full video export through the editor UI. If an export ever misbehaves,
# `npm install vite@^5` + deleting this file reverts, at the cost of the advisory.
legacy-peer-deps=true
